 Now I have started working on the fetcher part i do not know much about the fetcher so i have decided to first learn about it. As instructed there are two type of pages static and dynamic, in dynamic pages the page content is not inside the html tag when it return but the content loads on the client side after the page is return.Therefore for starting I have decided to make the fetcher to only load static html pages

 I am going to use libcurl for this and I am learning about it.
 I am able to create a basic libcurl implementation which store the html of the given URL into a string.For creating this I used curl_easy_interface, curl_easy_interface is used for data transfer over network it is synchoronous means it just block the process until the process is completed.
 First I generate a handle using curl_easy_init() which is pointer of CURL the CURL object will created in the heap and have all the config for network transfer, we can't directly access its member so we use public API like curl_easy_setopt() to set out option.
 The one most important option is the CURLOPT_URL by which we pass the URL to the object.The other important option are CURLOPT_WRITEFUNCTION and CURLOPT_WRITEDATA if we didn't set this option and call curl_easy_perform() the data from the url is going to be pasted on the terminal.

