I have implemented the fetcher.h and fetcher.cpp file after that I wrote a simple code for testing the fetcher in the main and use CMakeLists to compile it into a main executable file but I face this error 
 ![cmake can't find curl](image.png)

 Actually this is not a compiler error but a linker error it tells that the linker sees the declaration of these function in the curl/curl.h but could not find their implementation.

 Solution -> The simple solution is to add the line target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE CURL::libcurl)
 inside the CMakeLists.txt so that linker combine the implemenation from this external library

 Another error I face just after that 

 It happen because I need to call find_package(CURL REQUIRED) before target_link_libraries().

 Solution -> Added the find_package(CURL REQUIRED) line in CMakeLists.txt

